P1 mutual exclusion: yes, Forward=(dir=1), Reverse=(dir=-1). Branch interlock sets both false. P2 Stop or equal -> !Forward & !Reverse: desired=0, if previous_direction nonzero opposite? desired 0 not opposite, else outputs false and store 0. yes. P3 fwdOnly & qReverse -> neutral. fwdOnly means ForwardButton true, ReverseButton false, Stop false. qReverse from previous observed output O[k-1]. If qReverse true, previous_direction should be -1? Could qReverse true with previous_direction not -1? At end of any scan, if Reverse true then desired was -1, and code stores previous_direction=desired=-1 unless interlock branch? Interlock branch outputs false, so Reverse false. Thus qReverse true implies previous_direction=-1. So desired=+1 opposite, neutral. yes. P4 symmetrical. P5 fwdOnly & !qReverse -> Forward. If qReverse false, does code always output Forward? Need if previous_direction = -1 but qReverse false? Could previous_direction=-1 while previous output Reverse false? At end of scan with desired -1, output Reverse true, previous_direction=-1. At end with desired 0, previous_direction=0. At end with interlock neutral, previous_direction=0. So previous_direction=-1 implies qReverse true. Thus qReverse false implies previous_direction not -1. Could previous_direction +1 (same direction) -> output Forward true. Could previous_direction 0 -> output Forward true. Good. P6 symmetrical.

